WEBVTT

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:17.910
That dish has turmeric, pink peppercorns, cumin, coriander, and cloves.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:24.040
The right dish has amchoor, cardamom, dill, bay leaf, and savory.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:28.590
The left dish has star anise, fennel, wild yams, and lemon balm.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.170
You're amazing, Hayama-kun!

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:36.300
You identified all of them without being able to see or touch them!

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.970
Yeah, I'm perfectly ready.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.430
106... 107...

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:48.520
108... 109... 110...

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.360
111...

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.780
112...

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.200
Looks like he's perfectly ready.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.820
113...

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.530
114...

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:55.530
But...

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:56.240
Ugh!

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:57.490
You're covered in sweat!

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.030
Ryou-kun, you're nasty!

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:02.580
I wanted to ask you to clean my room.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.000
Go take a shower, already!

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.000
Miss!

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:05.540
Hm?

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:10.040
You're in a good mood, 
despite losing to Yukihira Souma.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:14.090
That's why you lost, probably.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.720
Hah, that's a poor attempt at provoking me,

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:18.970
but sure, I'll take it.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:22.270
Don't cry, even if you lose.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.360
I'll crush him!

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:34.820
I don't intend to lose 
to somebody else's <i>assistant</i>.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.660
<i>Hm, so those two are next.</i>

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.570
<i>I wonder how the match will go.</i>

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:42.330
Why are you here acting like you belong?!

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:46.080
Well, I was running late,
 and the match was about to start.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.460
Since I'll be facing whoever wins this round,

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.250
<i>Out! Get out! Go away!</i>

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.000
<i>Who do you think you are?!</i>

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:51.630
I need to get a good look.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.460
<i>You're just a two-bit chef.</i>

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:53.550
Huh?

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.550
Look who's with Nakiri-san.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:57.590
Souma-kun?

00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:58.430
What?

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:02.350
We'll now have the second match
 of the semi-finals!

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.350
The theme is the same
 as in the first match:

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.100
a Western-style main dish.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:08.900
Very well.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:11.480
Let the cooking...

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.570
commence!

00:02:15.990 --> 00:03:45.990
{OP}

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:40.640
Far beyond the image I have in my mind

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:47.110
The reality I'm building up is still far away

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:50.860
An endless journey

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:55.870
Let's hone each other's pride

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.370
Words aren't really important

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:00.870
So let's just say "yes" and leave it at that

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:07.840
We fight each other and hone our skills

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.720
Our encounters cause shockwaves

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.470
We're reckless challengers

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:20.470
Heading toward a world as yet unexplored

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.020
A swordsman should use his blade

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:25.850
To open the way to the future

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:31.570
This is my story and no one else's

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.250
Hayama's bringing out his ingredients.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.710
Is that chicken?

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:53.370
No.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:54.750
That's...

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:55.630
Duck!

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:01.760
His dish will depend on how well he takes advantage of duck's unique flavor profile.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.640
So he's Hayama Akira, the master of spices.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.890
He knows exactly what he's good at.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.220
A chef's sense of taste

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:12.560
is a compendium of all the flavors they've experienced in the past.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.770
It's cumulative.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:15.560
Yeah.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:20.940
If you can add a sense of smell that's keen enough to tell apart individual ingredients of various spice mixtures,

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.950
you've basically gained 
twice the momentum as a chef.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:26.320
<i>In addition to having a
 genius sense of smell,</i>

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:29.660
<i>he has been receiving the Tohtsuki education
 from his first year in junior high.</i>

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:32.620
<i>Hayama Akira is one of the super elite.</i>

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:36.420
<i>After Nakiri Alice, he's a top candidate to become a member of the Elite Ten.</i>

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:38.630
Hey, about this match.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:42.470
Yeah, the odds are 8 or 9 to 10
 that Hayama Akira will win.

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:43.300
Come to think of it,

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:48.220
according to Mitsuru, rumor has it that the students all favor Hayama to win.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.720
What do you think, Nakiri?

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:55.560
Well, I was once in the same 
class as Kurokiba-kun.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:05:01.440
The dishes he cooked up 
in that class were far from good.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.320
It wasn't enough to fail the class,

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.780
but the dishes lacked spirit,

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:10.120
as though they were made just well enough to pass the class.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:15.120
All the more reason that I was so surprised by his original creation in the preliminaries.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.670
Oh, that's why you're hopeless, Erina!

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:20.710
Excuse me!

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.800
Ryou-kun's true talent cannot
 be measured by logic alone.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.260
Eel?!

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:30.100
Seriously?

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.390
I'd heard seafood was his specialty,

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:34.680
but this is unexpected.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:37.270
Will he broil it Japanese-style?

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.360
Nah, the topic is Western cuisine.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:43.690
French and other foreign cuisines
 include dishes that use eel.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.820
It's not an ingredient limited 
to Japanese cuisine.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.280
<i>Eel.</i>

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:51.200
<i>Could he be trying to make...</i>

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.660
Hey, about what you said earlier,

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:54.830
what did you mean?

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:56.960
That logic isn't enough
 to measure his abilities.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.750
I didn't think that <i>you'd</i> talk about
 mind over matter, Alice.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:05.210
You're all about creating dishes
 using science and logic, aren't you?

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:07.720
This has nothing to do with "mind over matter."

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:13.680
It's just a fact that Ryou-kun's dishes are infused with something that goes beyond mere logic.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:15.310
<i>I have to win.</i>

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.520
<i>If I don't win,</i>

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.770
<i>I have nowhere I can call home!</i>

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.770
<i>If I don't win here,</i>

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:23.770
<i>I'll die!</i>

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:26.610
You see, Ryou-kun survived

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:30.030
in a kitchen straight out of hell.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:34.950
He only had his skills to rely on
 in a horrible environment.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:42.130
In order to live, Ryou-kun gained
 an absolute focus on taste,

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:45.420
and a fierce combativeness
 that smolders within him!

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:49.800
Ryou-kun and I have competed in cooking matches almost every day,

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:53.430
and he's never slacked off in any of them.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:55.140
Whenever he's in a match,

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.770
he's absolutely determined 
to shred you into pieces.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:03.480
If there is something I, myself,
 lack in a match, that would be...

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:06.190
Nope, never mind.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:10.240
<i>If there is something I lack,</i>

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:14.620
<i>it's a fierce obsession to win,
 an obsession as hot as molten lava!</i>

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:23.080
<i>If there's anyone here who has that in spades, 
it's Ryou-kun. I'm sure of it.</i>

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:26.710
An eel knife! It's a special knife for filleting eel.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:29.800
So he's well-versed in Japanese
 culinary techniques, as well.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:35.510
<i>This face-off is reminiscent of a match between a
 Stellar's sea eagle that has always flown high above,</i>

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:39.230
<i>and a vicious tiger who seeks to drag
 its prey down to the ground with its jaws!</i>

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:45.860
I don't sense any heat from you
 about our battle. I don't like that.

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:49.110
This is war!

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:51.490
Get out if you're not gunning to win.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.070
You're right.

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:58.290
I may not be as focused on winning as you.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:01.080
But the reason for that is simple.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:02.830
With my sense of smell,

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:05.710
it's hard to imagine how 
I could lose against you.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:06.790
What did you say?!

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:09.960
Now...

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:13.800
sound the ultimate melody of fragrance.

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.180
The fragrance of spices and
 the duck are intertwined!

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:19.470
It's unbelievable!

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:26.730
He's using coriander, fennel, oregano, and...

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:30.780
I can't tell! It's too complex!

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:35.110
How can you create such a wonderful aroma?

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:37.660
It's spicy, yet mellow.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:39.580
Faintly sweet, yet fragrant.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:42.960
You can practically feel the presence of royalty.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:46.830
In this moment, he dominates this space.

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:49.590
What's with him?

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.420
Where did all his energy go?

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:54.880
Was he discouraged by the 
applause for his opponent?

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.260
He doesn't even hear the audience.

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.600
Right now, Ryou-kun's only sensing

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.060
the degree of browning of the eel,

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:03.770
the sizzling sound and smell of fat,

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.140
and the weight of the eel.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:07.610
He's focused only on what's 
happening in the pan.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:10.480
<i>Kick all my senses into full throttle.</i>

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:12.940
<i>Don't miss the exact moment when the eel's
 reached cooked perfection!</i>

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:14.200
<i>Come!</i>

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:15.070
<i>Come!</i>

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:15.950
<i>Come!</i>

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:17.360
<i>Now!</i>

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:18.870
<i>It's done!</i>

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:21.830
Like I thought, Kurokiba-kun's 
going for matelote.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:23.620
Matelote?

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:26.290
It's a cooking method where fish 
is braised with wine.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:27.040
Huh.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:28.210
Oh?

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.460
Wait, though he split the eel open,

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:32.000
he put it back together.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:37.090
He wrapped the eel in caul fat to restore its original shape before cooking it.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:42.140
Caul fat's the mesh-like thing that
 covers beef and pork organs, right?

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.060
That's right.

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:46.350
The fat adds richness of flavor,
 increasing the dish's impact.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:48.560
It's a very Ryou-kun thing to do.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:54.940
Fluffy mashed potatoes 
and home-made brioche.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:59.950
So he deals out the many cards at his disposal to overwhelm his opponents.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:03.540
That's how he's been constructing the destructive power of his dishes.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:08.000
You can try to win over the audience with your aroma theatrics as much as you want,

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.880
but I don't give a shit.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:11.840
I'll just tear right through it!

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:16.970
I have my own cards too.

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:20.340
Besides, what's the point 
of having a lot of cards

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:23.180
if you can't master them?

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.810
Hayama's always been calm before.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.600
Now he's like a totally different person!

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:31.440
He's never had to show his claws before,

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.360
but now he finally has.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:34.780
That's what his laugh seems to say.

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:38.950
It's done.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:41.570
Candidate Hayama is first to serve his dish!

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:45.240
Its rich aroma has already enveloped the arena!

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:48.210
Here is my dish, Canard Apicius.

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:54.880
It's the dish said to have been beloved by Apicius,
 a gourmand in Roman times.

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:58.050
It glistens from the caramelized honey.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:01.640
The spices sprinkled across 
the duck meat are very fragrant.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:04.350
The aroma's enough to make you melt.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:07.810
What will happen once you take an actual bite?!

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:10.190
Let's have a taste.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:21.450
What a gorgeous and spicy aroma piercing through my body!

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:23.780
Even after you've chewed 
and swallowed the bite,

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:26.660
the fragrance continues to spread throughout your nose and mouth!

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:29.120
I'm so happy!

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:31.120
What an unbelievable 
combination of fragrances!

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:32.880
<i>I've been seized by</i>

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.880
<i>the talons of aroma magic!</i>

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:40.510
<i>Though we lump them together as spices,
 each has unique characteristics that are limitless.</i>

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:42.720
<i>Some are quite hot,</i>

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:44.220
<i>others faintly sweet.</i>

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:46.260
<i>Some are refreshing and astringent,</i>

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:48.140
<i>while others are bitter.</i>

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:51.390
<i>This dish demonstrates full command of their delicate power balance.</i>

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:54.560
<i>It would not be possible without his sense of smell!</i>

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:56.770
Full frontal assault!

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:03.570
Fragrance is what will rule the culinary world.

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:06.370
No matter how many cards
 you may add to your deck,

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:09.160
your cards would never be my equal.

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:12.460
Kurokiba's eyes...

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.040
What?

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:15.040
They haven't lost all hope.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.340
Hayama Akira.

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:20.340
I finally sense the heat of battle within you.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:23.050
<i>It wouldn't be worth fighting back otherwise!</i>

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:27.260
The challenger is Candidate Kurokiba!

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:31.600
What ace does he have up his sleeve as a specialist in seafood cuisine?

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:33.480
Have a taste!

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:35.940
My dish is Eel Matelote!

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.020
Oh, my!

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:39.860
What a massive portion size!

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:44.200
The use of caul fat during the cooking process has heightened the eel's juiciness!

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:44.490
Hmph.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:47.660
In terms of the aroma, he falls far short.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.040
No one who's all bark and no bite
 can serve a decent dish—

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:53.460
Quit yappin' and eat before it gets cold.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:54.460
Oh?

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:57.880
What the hell?! Want me
 to teach you some manners?!

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:00.420
If you think you can act up
 just because you're a student,

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.840
I can teach you different right here, right now!

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:02.840
Stay calm, Taki-senpai!

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:03.800
Stay calm!

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.010
Now, let's have a taste.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:09.140
Oh, my! The eel has been simmered
 through. It's so tender.

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:13.060
The eel was marinated in red wine with cinnamon before it was cooked,

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.730
which imparts a fresh flavor.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:17.230
I've rigged the eel with explosives.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:21.440
It's got a detonation device designed to blow you out of the running!

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:26.530
<i>What is it?</i>

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:29.530
<i>What's this electrifying jolt in my mouth?!</i>

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:32.950
In the eel, Kurokiba hid...

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.040
a surprise! Plums!

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:38.460
Plums?

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:39.420
Japanese plums?!

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.170
He paired plums with eel?!

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:47.630
<i>The slick eel fat has been infused
 with the plums' fruity acidity,</i>

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.550
<i>creating a taste sensation
 that goes right to your brain!</i>

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:52.720
I'm numb.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:55.600
The eel was stuffed with reconstituted dried plums,

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:57.440
then wrapped with caul fat.

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:59.190
So that's what you meant.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:02.400
It's an explosion of acidity from the plums.

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:03.900
Shut up and watch.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:05.530
Next!

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:08.240
Take the brioche and mashed potatoes

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:13.330
and dip them into the sauce that's full of umami from the simmered eel.

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:17.330
Make sure to add some of the eel flesh, and shove the whole package into your mouth!

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:20.000
Keep on eating, with no shame,

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.210
until you can't stand up anymore.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:23.840
<i>Damn!</i>

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:26.550
<i>This is a festival of gourmet food
 at Tohtsuki Academy!</i>

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:29.050
<i>He should try to be more civil!</i>

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:30.720
<i>But!</i>

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:34.720
This is where things will really explode!

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:43.480
<i>The mashed potatoes' entangling texture...</i>

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.440
<i>The fluffy brioche...</i>

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:48.150
<i>The eel's sweet fat and the plums' acidity...</i>

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:50.450
<i>They're all rioting in my mouth!</i>

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:53.530
<i>All the flavors are melding
 into one harmonious whole!</i>

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:58.500
<i>This is different from Hayama Akira's bewitching flavors 
that threaten to take you to nirvana.</i>

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.750
<i>This is an explosive burst
 meant to pierce any defense!</i>

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:03.960
<i>Flavors so delicious that they subdue all prey!</i>

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:06.090
<i>Shit. I can't resist!</i>

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:08.920
<i>I am a lesser being before him.</i>

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:11.390
<i>I have become the prey!</i>

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:13.720
I bet you thought you had won.

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:15.890
Caught you!

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:20.810
This concludes the evaluation!

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:22.520
Time for the final assessment.

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:25.770
Judges, please cast your vote for the
 candidate who served the better dish!

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:34.200
The vote's finally starting.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:35.120
But...

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.660
The judges are paralyzed.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:40.660
Until now, all the matches have
 been decided right away.

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:44.460
Our alums are having trouble deciding, despite all the experience they have?

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:48.920
I've decided!

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:50.920
I believe my vote is for Hayama-kun!

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:55.010
I vote for Hayama Akira, as well.

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:55.800
He's got two votes.

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:56.760
So Hayama's the stronger candidate.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:57.720
Maybe it's decided, then.

00:15:57.720 --> 00:15:59.220
So it's Hayama, after all.

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:01.350
His dish was impressive.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:06.610
I believe my vote is for Kurokiba Ryou.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:07.980
But why?

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:11.070
His dish's rich flavors leveraged
 the seafood's potential.

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:15.450
I saw sophistication in that 
masculine, destructive flavor!

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:19.620
I judge his dish to be worthy of 
acknowledgment in the Autumn Selection.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:23.620
<i>Which one should it be?</i>

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:27.460
<i>Both expressed their individuality in their dish.</i>

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:31.470
<i>But the one whose dish had the greater impact was...</i>

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:33.970
Shit!

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:35.680
I also vote for Kurokiba Ryou!

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:39.680
This is unbelievable.

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:41.350
It's a split vote.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:43.940
This is almost like a Cooking Battle!

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:44.520
Yeah.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:48.230
It all hangs on Chef Kikuchi Sonoka's vote.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:58.990
I can't decide.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:03.290
Each dish was superb.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:06.000
I can't rank one over the other.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:07.750
Cut the bullshit!

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:09.920
This is a match!

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:12.420
It's not over until one of us falls!

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:14.680
Get your act together and decide!

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:17.430
What's the meaning of this, judge?

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:18.470
Make up your mind!

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:20.890
Are you mocking a serious competition?!

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:23.930
I can understand where she's coming from.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:27.270
The two are so equally matched.

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:28.560
Organizers, a word.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:30.770
What is it, Chef Doujima?

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:31.900
Huh?

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:33.240
When'd they leave?

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:35.450
If this were a Cooking Battle,

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:37.610
and a final decision could not be reached,

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:41.540
there would be a rematch at a later date to determine the final outcome,

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:42.240
am I right?

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:44.120
That's correct.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:46.250
But this is the Autumn Selection.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:51.840
Our honored guests and the judges all have very busy schedules.

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:57.840
Pragmatically speaking, it would be impossible to schedule a rematch, unfortunately.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:17:59.640
Given that, I have a suggestion.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:03.890
There is one way to resolve this dilemma.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.190
Let both of them proceed.

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:13.230
I propose that there be a three-way final round
 for the very first time in the Autumn Selections!

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:14.690
What?!

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:16.240
A three-way?!

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:19.610
But there is no precedent!

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:21.660
The judges cannot simply decide to—

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:24.450
That's an interesting proposal!

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:29.580
I will approve it with my authority as the director of this academy!

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:34.090
Kurokiba Ryou and Hayama Akira's match is determined to be a draw!

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:37.050
Both will proceed to the final round!

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:42.510
Yukihira Souma will join
 the two of them in the final match!

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:50.900
Candidate Kurokiba, congratulations for proceeding to the final round.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:52.610
Um, any thoughts on moving forward?

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:55.030
Congratulations, my ass!

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:56.990
I haven't accepted this result!

00:18:56.990 --> 00:19:03.700
They only delayed the outcome, you little shits!

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:03.700
Ryou-kun! Heel! Heel!

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.870
Well, let's see.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:08.660
I regret that Candidate Kurokiba
 and I fought to a draw,

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:12.290
but I'd like to switch gears and
 prepare for my next match.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:13.880
Yukihira-senpai!

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:17.010
Senpai, please tell us your thoughts moving forward to the final match too.

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:18.760
Huh? I have to say something?

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:21.220
This is kind of awkward.

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:25.350
Uh... Well, in the prelims, I was in the same group as those two.

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:29.680
Hayama beat me by one point, 
and Kurokiba scored the same as me.

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:33.690
I've wanted to defeat both of them fair and square before moving on up,

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:38.190
so I feel lucky to have this chance.

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:43.620
We now conclude the semi-finals.

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:49.080
Next, the organizers will announce 
the theme for the finals!

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:50.410
Oh?

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:53.830
Every year, the finals have a seasonal ingredient as their theme.

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:58.300
It's considered only appropriate as a choice to conclude the Autumn Selection.

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:04.390
The topic is Pacific saury.

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:06.470
In olden times,

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:10.230
it was considered lowbrow fish,
 eaten only by the common masses.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:13.150
But in recent years, it has been served in high-end restaurants

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:16.190
and made appearances in restaurants overseas.

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:21.110
A dish using this fish will be
 the theme of the final round.

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:22.360
Hayama Akira.

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:23.820
Kurokiba Ryou.

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:25.450
Yukihira Souma.

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:29.740
I feel fate's strange hand at work because
 these three are advancing to the final round.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:33.500
For Pacific saury is an extremely <i>fragrant</i> fish,

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:35.500
a highly valued <i>seafood</i> ingredient,

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.250
and a fish with deep ties
 to the <i>common people's table</i>!{pls try shorten}

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:42.470
It is therefore an ingredient that allows each of you to capitalize on your own strengths!

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:44.550
The finals will be held in ten days.

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:48.390
I trust that it will be the ultimate battle!

00:20:49.060 --> 00:22:19.060
{ED}

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:18.130
An intensely burning desire was born

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:23.970
But not in me, in someone else

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:28.770
Where's the me who believed that

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:33.900
All one needs is to have hopes and dreams

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:39.150
Wrapped around something long, my compass was lost

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:44.910
On the border of life and death, snow drops bloom

00:21:44.910 --> 00:21:50.250
If by some mistake they get smashed

00:21:50.250 --> 00:21:55.420
At least put flowers on the empty husk

00:21:55.420 --> 00:22:01.090
Is that the way things are? Yes, it is

00:22:01.090 --> 00:22:06.140
You can call it resignation if you want

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:12.060
But that's not me, that's not me

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:16.690
There's no value in something just anyone could make

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:20.980
Hayama-kun!

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:22.730
Hayama-kun!

00:22:23.150 --> 00:22:24.400
The finals!

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:26.440
I know. Calm down, Jun.

00:22:26.440 --> 00:22:29.780
C'mon, how can you stay so calm?

00:22:29.780 --> 00:22:32.160
I'm so happy for you!

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:34.370
Sorry, let me go blow my nose!

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:36.200
Yeah, Hayama.

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:41.040
You should stop trying to put up a calm front and let yourself be frustrated.

00:22:41.040 --> 00:22:43.250
There's nothing to be frustrated about.

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:44.130
Oh?

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:49.340
My plans to advance to the finals and then win the Autumn Selection are still on schedule.

00:22:50.390 --> 00:22:52.350
Even though our match was a draw,

00:22:52.350 --> 00:22:55.180
you're still putting on airs, spice bastard?

00:22:55.600 --> 00:22:58.810
You're only good at using spices.
 You're a one-trick pony.

00:22:58.810 --> 00:23:01.190
I see right through all your cards now.

00:23:01.190 --> 00:23:02.770
I'll get you next time.

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:05.480
You too, Yukihira.

00:23:06.610 --> 00:23:07.740
What are you doing?

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:08.950
Let's go home.

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:10.320
Oh...

00:23:10.320 --> 00:23:11.360
Excuse us.

00:23:11.740 --> 00:23:13.120
Later. Good work.

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:15.200
<i>Don't deflate without warning like that.</i>

00:23:15.200 --> 00:23:17.620
<i>I can't keep up with all the mood swings.</i>

00:23:18.370 --> 00:23:19.830
Later, Yukihira.

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:22.290
Enjoy grinning while you still can.

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:27.510
Miss, can you fight me in a cooking match as soon as we get back?

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:33.800
I don't think I'll be able to sleep until the final round, because there's no closure.

00:23:34.510 --> 00:23:37.060
<i>So I'm only good at using spices?</i>

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:38.180
Today's semi-finals were amazing!

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:45.230
<i>Fine, I'll show you, then.</i>

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:48.820
<i>The true world where fragrance beckons.</i>

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:51.360
<i>The final round, huh.</i>

00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:53.370
<i>I finally got here.</i>

00:23:54.030 --> 00:23:56.830
<i>No, this is just the beginning.</i>

00:23:57.490 --> 00:24:01.540
<i>Let's go see how things look higher up!</i>

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:11.050
Next time, "Battle of Seasonality."
